# Logging

Use `core.enterprise_logging`. Do not add a logging package. `core/logging.py` is not a module in this repo. `core/structured_logging.py` is legacy; do not point new calls at it.

When a log line is structured, include event, service, severity, and trace_id. Add user_id when the request has one. LLM lines include latency_ms and cost_usd when those values exist.

Do not log secrets, raw tokens, full email bodies, or full prompts and responses that contain personal data. Prefer an id or a short summary.

Read this file before adding logs in another module. The glob attaches when the logger itself is open.
